<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fascist Italy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1922–1943</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Kingdom of Italy under Fascism</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fascist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-italy">Kingdom of Italy</a> under the dictatorship of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benito-mussolini">Benito Mussolini</a>, from his appointment as prime minister in 1922 to his fall in 1943. The regime suppressed opposition, reconquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/libya">Libya</a>, invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a> in 1935 and aided Franco in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-civil-war">Spanish Civil War</a>. It joined Nazi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>, which brought its collapse.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fascist-italy.jpg" alt="Fascist Italy" width="320" height="435" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Keystone-France/Gamma-Keystone · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Benito_Mussolini_1930.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
